   "glasses": true,
   "extra": "moustache"
  },
  "script": "Lightbulbs aren't the only thing built to cheat. In 2015, researchers at West Virginia University tested Volkswagen diesels on real roads. In the lab, they were clean. On the road, they pumped out up to forty times the legal limit of nitrogen oxides. The cars could tell when they were being tested. Eleven million of them. It cost Volkswagen billions. So when someone tells you a thing passed the test, ask which test."
